%% Concurrency-driven autoscaling — Serverless Zero-to-Hero, lab exercise 3 ("You'll end with").
%% Twelve requests in flight against containerConcurrency 2 ask for six pods; max-scale 3 caps the
%% revision at three; when the load stops the pods are removed and the service returns to zero.
%% Shape (diagram-size-guard): LR, longest chain 4 nodes, no subgraph, labels at most 2 lines.
flowchart LR
  LOAD(["12 requests<br/>in flight"]) --> KPA["autoscaler<br/>2 requests per pod"]
  KPA --> PODS["pods<br/>0 → 3"]
  CAP["max-scale 3"] -.->|"caps"| PODS
  PODS -->|"load stops"| ZERO["back to<br/>0 pods"]
  classDef hi fill:#e00,stroke:#900,color:#fff;
  classDef plat fill:#f3f3f3,stroke:#888,color:#333;
  class KPA,PODS hi;
  class LOAD,CAP,ZERO plat;
